From 14f37c25d08fd459623c327b3139158a7fde887b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Red <235753003+ban-red@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:33:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hw/input/hid: queue up to 256 events instead of 16

hid_keyboard_event drops an event when the queue is full, and the guest
drains it one event per USB poll. Input from a remote viewer can arrive
in bursts (network jitter, a paste typed as keystrokes); with 16 slots
a burst overflows, and when the dropped event is a key release the
guest auto-repeats that key until it is pressed again.

Raise QUEUE_LENGTH to 256: a burst is then delayed by a few polls
rather than lost. The pointer queue shares the constant; its motion is
already merged into the previous event, so it only fills with button
changes, which it now keeps instead of dropping. This changes the size
of the arrays in the migration stream.
---
 include/hw/input/hid.h | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/hw/input/hid.h b/include/hw/input/hid.h
index 6a9d7bf..2f4587b 100644
--- a/include/hw/input/hid.h
+++ b/include/hw/input/hid.h
@@ -12,7 +12,14 @@ typedef struct HIDPointerEvent {
     int32_t dz, buttons_state;
 } HIDPointerEvent;
 
-#define QUEUE_LENGTH    16 /* should be enough for a triple-click */
+/*
+ * Enough for a burst of keystrokes: a remote viewer's input can arrive in
+ * clumps (network jitter), and the guest drains one event per USB poll.
+ * A full queue drops events, a lost key-up leaves the key held and the
+ * guest repeating it.  Must stay a power of two (QUEUE_MASK).  Changes the
+ * migration stream's array sizes.
+ */
+#define QUEUE_LENGTH    256
 #define QUEUE_MASK      (QUEUE_LENGTH-1u)
 #define QUEUE_INCR(v)   ((v)++, (v) &= QUEUE_MASK)
 
